      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The arguments regarding grid reliability focus on the rapid, necessary overhaul required to support a high influx of variable renewable power like solar and wind.\n\nThe concerns for heavy industry center on the increased capital and operational costs associated with adhering to new clean energy requirements, which some argue could lead to \"de-industrialization\" in the US.\n\nThese arguments have some weight, particularly in the short term, as the necessary infrastructure build-out *is* a complex and massive undertaking that needs careful planning to avoid market strain or competitive disadvantage for certain strong, energy-intensive sectors right now.",
